From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jcode patch catalog <jcode@localhost>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 22:07:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: remove hosted subscription and promotional commands

X-Jcode-Patch-Intent: Remove standalone hosted subscription commands, sales pitches, rate-limit upsells, and promotional UI surfaces.
X-Jcode-Patch-Kind: personal-feature
X-Jcode-Patch-Depends-On: 1007-personal-feature-disable-telemetry-delivery-and-remove-telemetry-controls.patch

Patch intent:
Remove standalone hosted subscription commands, sales pitches, rate-limit
upsells, and promotional UI surfaces from the CLI and TUI.

Why it exists:
This personal build must not promote, upsell, or direct users to buy or
manage a hosted plan. Configured inference routes and manual provider login
remain available without commercial encouragement.

Upstream integration points:
The patch relies on the CLI command registry, TUI command dispatch,
authentication command wiring, and command help surfaces.

Update guidance:
Remove upstream hosted service promotions, subscription commands, and upsell
text while retaining ordinary provider configuration, manual login, and jcode
inference dispatch.

Validation:
scripts/cargo_exec.sh check -p jcode -p jcode-tui
scripts/cargo_exec.sh test -p jcode-tui command_palette_omits_hosted_subscription_promotions --lib
